NEW TO MARKET in Observatory Circle! 3400 Massachusetts Ave, NW, a rare Washington estate defined by its presence.

Offered at $10,250,000.

Prominently sited in prestigious Observatory Circle, the historic Heurich-Parks House at 3400 Massachusetts Ave, NW presents a rare opportunity to own a fully reconstructed Washington estate. Originally built in 1925 by architect Albert S.J. Atkinson and once home to Christian Heurich Jr., a philanthropic businessman, as well as Marshall Parks, known as the "father of pediatric ophthalmology," this distinguished Spanish Mission-style residence was masterfully reconstructed and expanded in 2017 with designs by renowned BarnesVanze Architects, seamlessly blending historic provenance with modern luxury. Set on a beautifully landscaped and level 0.39-acre lot with irrigation, the property is introduced by a grand circular driveway and features a detached 2-car garage with guest house studio above. Encompassing approximately 13,900 square feet, the residence offers 7 bedrooms, 9 full baths, 2 half baths, and an elevator.

